User: *Gen4 RichMenu Has Arrived in @crysnovax/baileys*


We are excited to announce the arrival of Gen4 RichMenu in `@crysnovax/baileys`.This feature began with a request from `@pappy`, who challenged us to reproduce the rich, Meta AI-style menu experience: a large media header, card-based layouts, quick-reply buttons, URL actions, multiple menu columns, and a polished channel-style footer.We did not stop at surface-level imitation. The implementation was developed through protocol research and comparative analysis with `@Rajeh Taher`, the German owner and maintainer associated with `@vansnowi/baileys v1.5.7`. By studying the underlying message structures and GenAI rich-response envelope, we were able to build a practical, reusable API for developers using `@crysnovax/baileys`.

```What Gen4 RichMenu supports```

Gen4 RichMenu can combine 
- a title, 
- optional image,
-  card rows or
-  carousel layouts,
-  quick-reply buttons,
-  button identifiers,
- optional toast metadata,
-  disclaimers, and
-  a URL-based footer action in one rich response. 

The message is serialized through the compatible botForwardedMessage and richResponseMessage structure used by WhatsApp’s richer response formats.A basic example looks like this:
```
await sock.richMenu(jid, {
  header: {
    title: 'Rich Menu',
    image: {
      url: 'https://example.com/menu.jpg',
      mime_type: 'image/jpeg'
    }
  },
  body: {
    row: true,
    cards: [
      {
        title: 'Menu 1',
        buttons: ['menu2', 'menu3', 'rich3']
      },
      {
        title: 'Menu 2',
        buttons: ['test', 'me', 'rich2']
      }
    ]
  },
  footer: {
    text: 'Telegram channel',
    url: 'https://t.me/example'
  }
});
```

The result is a structured rich menu with interactive card actions rather than a plain text menu. Developers can use the button identifiers to connect the interface to their own command handlers, navigation logic, AI tools, or application workflows.Built for developersGen4 RichMenu is now part of the broader rich-response direction of `@crysnovax/baileys`. It is designed to work alongside existing support for tables, code blocks, rich grids, native flows, media, status features, and other message helpers.The implementation includes public TypeScript declarations, documentation, a dedicated builder, and regression tests covering the GenAI image, card, button, footer, and forwarding envelope structures.From a community request to a tested developer feature: Gen4 RichMenu brings a new level of interactive presentation to `@crysnovax/baileys.`

Thanks to `@pappy` for the original request  and to @Rajeh Taher for the research collaboration and comparative insight that helped guide this implementation.
